    "name": "Pink Raspberries",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">The term </span><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">\"pink raspberry\"</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">typically refers to specific hybrid varieties of the fruit (like </span><i><em class=\"lexical-text-editor--italic\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Candy Pink</em></i><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">), a culinary description of a light, bright pink color, or the immature stage of standard red raspberries. Standard fresh raspberries are actually red with pink undertones, though unripe or \"frosted\" berries can appear almost completely pink. </span></p><p><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Grown by: Various NW Growers</span></p>",
